BCA's penalty: the consistent and exceptional cases, rebuilt from recorded inputs (nothing trained, no band fitted).
repository root M:\; numpy 2.5.4

==============================================================================================================
Case 1 [consistent]: the standard penalty is the same number whatever the test condition (dose and width)
==============================================================================================================
Before = the dose on the recorded training rows; after = the same dose read under a shifted test. The dose is read
at recorded (state, command) rows from a threshold fixed at the last refresh (calibration/dose.py:65-95,
algorithms/td3_bc_bca.py:283-288), so a shift in the test states cannot reach it. What the records show:

  (a) Weighting test, capped pull, seed 0, standard arm: mean dose per 5,000 updates after the first refresh
      (outputs/shift_iw/explore/routes2/diagnose/dose_chunks.json; exploratory)
      random         min 1.318  mean 1.329  max 1.343  last 1.343  (18 chunks)
      medium-replay  min 1.317  mean 1.327  max 1.337  last 1.336  (18 chunks)
      medium         min 1.315  mean 1.327  max 1.341  last 1.341  (18 chunks)
      medium-expert  min 1.293  mean 1.307  max 1.327  last 1.316  (18 chunks)
      expert         min 1.297  mean 1.309  max 1.321  last 1.318  (18 chunks)

  (b) The same band read at four commands of the recorded state (dose-equivalent 1 + 0.5 U/(U+u); seed 0;
      diag_band_at_commands.json): recorded command | actor's command | 60% hold | 80% hold | full throttle
      random         1.3568  1.3550  1.3545  1.3543  1.3542   spread 0.0026
      medium-replay  1.3501  1.3478  1.3470  1.3464  1.3460   spread 0.0041
      medium         1.3590  1.3572  1.3566  1.3562  1.3561   spread 0.0029
      medium-expert  1.3408  1.3389  1.3404  1.3398  1.3400   spread 0.0019
      expert         1.3241  1.3247  1.3221  1.3235  1.3247   spread 0.0026

  (c) Four-learner study, standard arm, mean dose on kept training rows at the last refresh, per seed
      (origin/claude/shift-hosts:outputs/shift_hosts_v3/results.json; exploratory seeds 0-4)
      cql     medium         mean dose per seed [1.347, 1.352, 1.373, 1.352, 1.361]  rows' min 1.009 max 1.451
      rebrac  medium         mean dose per seed [1.347, 1.307, 1.299, 1.319, 1.354]  rows' min 1.191 max 1.379
      td3_bc  medium-expert  mean dose per seed [1.357, 1.360, 1.368, 1.367, 1.362]  rows' min 1.277 max 1.407
      cql     medium-expert  mean dose per seed [1.340, 1.340, 1.385, 1.359, 1.336]  rows' min 1.008 max 1.458

  Count: every recorded standard dose level lies in [1.293, 1.385] (110 readings: 90 chunk means + 20 seed means); the dose at the
  actor's full-throttle command differs from the recorded command's by at most 0.0041 (5 qualities).
  Takeaway: the standard penalty cannot be 'higher under shift' because it never looks at the test condition.

