  Count: CQL's dose rises on 10 of 10 seeds (+0.125 to +0.156); ReBRAC (critic did not learn): case 10.
  Takeaway: declared weights raise the penalty everywhere, by 1.1-2.3x in the threshold and 0.02-0.16 in the dose.

==============================================================================================================
Case 6 [consistent]: weights of 1 (the IID test declared exactly) give the standard penalty bit for bit
==============================================================================================================
Before = standard calibrate(scores); after = calibrate(scores, weights = 1, test mass = 1), same random stream
(calibration/wbcp.py:62-66 and :117; experiments/shift_iw/coverage.py:78-86 unit_check).
  weighting test W0 random        : unit check [True, True, True, True, True] (gapped host), [True, True, True, True, True] (full host); status pass
  weighting test W0 medium-replay : unit check [True, True, True, True, True] (gapped host), [True, True, True, True, True] (full host); status pass
  weighting test W0 medium        : unit check [True, True, True, True, True] (gapped host), [True, True, True, True, True] (full host); status pass
  weighting test W0 medium-expert : unit check [True, True, True, True, True] (gapped host), [True, True, True, True, True] (full host); status pass
  weighting test W0 expert        : unit check [True, True, True, True, True] (gapped host), [True, True, True, True, True] (full host); status pass
  Count: 50 of 50 seed-hosts identical (threshold, lambda_hat, lambda_hpd, every posterior crossing, the per-step
  table [1.0] and the per-step arm's coverage). Pre-registered mark W0 (labeled a unit check).
  Four-learner stop rule S2 (PRESPEC.md:474): IW with every weight 1 equals the standard run in every bit after the
  refresh, and R(1) equals the stored standard threshold in float32: passed for all four learners (the study ran on).
  live near-80 version 6 near80 no_stall seed 0: recorded R 1.533197; weights of 1 -> 1.533197; equals recorded recompute True; explicit ones bit-equal True
  Recorded held-out scores (pinned environment, data/penalty_recompute.json): 30 of 30 banks reproduce the
  recorded threshold, and weights of 1 equal the unweighted call bit for bit on 30 of 30.
  Takeaway: with no shift and known weights the weighted penalty cannot differ from the standard one.

==============================================================================================================
Case 7 [exceptional]: estimated weights fitted for the IID test move the threshold by -9% to +5% on single seeds
==============================================================================================================
Before = standard R_u; after = R with the classifier's weights fitted on the IID ('none') mix, where the exact weights
are 1 (single threshold at the frozen band; shown values; the classifier is logistic regression on the 13-number
observation, experiments/shift_iw/classifier.py). Also its fitted slope on the current (exact 0; mark W4) and the
coverage of the estimated band minus the exact one on the IID test.
