  Count: IW higher than standard on 14 of 25 seed-qualities, lower on 9, equal on 2; beyond 1% on 12, beyond 5% on
  2 (both medium-expert: seed 2 at 0.913, seed 4 at 1.050). The sign of the move agrees with the sign of the fitted
  slope on the current in 20 of 23 moved cases: a positive slope tilts the weights toward high-current rows, where
  the scores are larger (mark M2), so the weighted quantile rises; a negative slope lowers it. Means by quality are
  within 1% of 1 (W4's coverage gap 0.0001-0.002). Exceptional: classifier noise on a slope whose true value is 0.
  The same 25 slopes applied to random currents on the 30 recorded banks (no link between weight and score; pinned
  recompute case E): R ratio 0.930 to 1.033, beyond 5% in 2 of 3000. So the recorded moves beyond 5%
  need the weights to be correlated with the scores (the tilt), not the smaller effective sample.

==============================================================================================================
Case 8 [consistent]: weights for the strong shift, applied while the learner trains on IID rows, raise the penalty on every seed
==============================================================================================================
This is how the IW arm is actually run: its band is calibrated for the strong test law, and the dose it reads on the
recorded (IID) training rows is therefore higher than the standard arm's. Before = standard, after = IW.
  (a) Weighting test, seed 0, mean dose per 5,000-update chunk after the first refresh, IW arm minus standard arm
      (dose_chunks.json, exploratory; two different training runs):
      random         IW - standard per chunk: min +0.0125 mean +0.0250 max +0.0367; per-row R_w/R_u at the first two refreshes: [1.155, 1.212], [1.358, 1.380]
      medium-replay  IW - standard per chunk: min +0.0169 mean +0.0268 max +0.0406; per-row R_w/R_u at the first two refreshes: [1.318, 1.370], [1.340, 1.403]
      medium         IW - standard per chunk: min +0.0225 mean +0.0307 max +0.0463; per-row R_w/R_u at the first two refreshes: [1.532, 1.663], [1.256, 1.323]
      medium-expert  IW - standard per chunk: min +0.0415 mean +0.0603 max +0.0846; per-row R_w/R_u at the first two refreshes: [2.200, 2.367], [1.578, 1.951]
      expert         IW - standard per chunk: min +0.0130 mean +0.0445 max +0.0607; per-row R_w/R_u at the first two refreshes: [1.314, 1.503], [1.639, 1.744]
      Count: IW's dose is above the standard arm's in 90 of 90 chunks (5 qualities x 18 chunks), and every per-row
      threshold ratio at the recorded refreshes is above 1 (10 of 10 refresh records).
  (b) The frozen band: R2's dose change (case 5) is positive on 25 of 25 seeds; CQL's on 10 of 10; refused rows 0 everywhere.
  (c) What it costs where there is no shift (return on the IID starts, IW minus standard; exploratory):
      random         capped pull: return units per seed [-7.7, 0.1, 4.0, 8.5, 1.5] (mean +1.3, +0.17 points); lower edge [-0.2, 1.7, -0.7, 1.2, 1.4]
      medium-replay  capped pull: return units per seed [-9.4, -1.0, -9.9, -20.3, -5.0] (mean -9.1, -1.19 points); lower edge [-0.2, 0.7, -0.7, 0.0, -0.1]
      medium         capped pull: return units per seed [-3.0, -11.0, -3.1, -4.4, -1.8] (mean -4.6, -0.61 points); lower edge [-0.4, -0.3, -0.3, -1.1, -0.1]
      medium-expert  capped pull: return units per seed [-0.7, -0.9, -0.6, 0.2, -0.6] (mean -0.5, -0.07 points); lower edge [0.1, 0.1, 0.1, 0.2, 0.3]
      expert         capped pull: return units per seed [-0.4, 0.1, -0.2, -1.3, 0.2] (mean -0.3, -0.04 points); lower edge [-0.1, -0.0, 0.1, -0.0, -0.1]
      four-learner CQL medium         claim 3 (IW - standard on the IID bank): [2.21, 0.24, -3.96, 0.49, -2.74] mean -0.75; passed
      four-learner CQL medium-expert  claim 3 (IW - standard on the IID bank): [4.45, -0.62, 0.31, 0.86, -2.75] mean +0.45; passed
      Count: the capped pull loses return on 18 of 25 IID seed-qualities (largest mean loss medium-replay, -9.1 units =
      -1.2 points); the lower edge and CQL stay within a few units either way.
  (d) Why the threshold rises: the three parts, on the 30 recorded banks (pinned recompute, data/penalty_recompute.json):
      B  test atom alone (mass 2.84 instead of 1, weights 1):          R_w/R_u mean 1.015
      C  strong weights on random currents (Kish 0.35 n, no link to the scores): mean 1.094, range 0.806-1.513; above 1 in 522 of 600 draws, below in 68
         weighted empirical quantile / unweighted 1.013; Bayesian margin lambda_hpd/lambda_hat 1.089 -> 1.175
      D  strong weights sorted onto the scores: heaviest on the largest scores 2.91x, on the smallest 0.43x
      F  the margin as the bank shrinks: n = 300 1.173, n = 100 1.498 (recorded n = 805-851: 1.089)
      The recorded strong ratios (1.11-2.25 per seed) sit far above C and below D-up: most of the rise is the reweighting
      toward the high-current rows, where the critic's scores are larger; the smaller effective sample adds about
      +9% to the threshold (+0.01 in the dose: the four-learner shuffled placebo -0.008 to +0.017).
      live near-80 version 6 near80 no_stall seed 0: B 1.0108, C strong mean 1.0713 [0.954, 1.247], D up 2.546, down 0.443
  Takeaway: the higher IW penalty under IID training rows is the declared shift, not a defect; it costs at most about 1 point.

==============================================================================================================
Case 9 [exceptional]: refusal (R = +inf): too few effective held-out rows, never the IW arms on record
==============================================================================================================
The credible quantile is finite only when at least 950 of the 1,000 posterior draws cross; a draw fails with
probability 0.9^n, so about 29 rows are needed (near80_results_check/REPORT.md:24-27; calibration/wbcp.py:108-117).
  (a) Every certificate with a full-throttle group of at most 30 rows (finite share = share of finite draws):
      near-80  main         no_stall  seed 10  n_tail 18  finite share 0.854 (1 - 0.9^n = 0.850)  height +inf  switch off
      near-80  main         stall     seed 13  n_tail 18  finite share 0.850 (1 - 0.9^n = 0.850)  height +inf  switch on
      near-80  main         stall     seed 10  n_tail 19  finite share 0.879 (1 - 0.9^n = 0.865)  height +inf  switch on
      near-80  main         no_stall  seed 12  n_tail 21  finite share 0.890 (1 - 0.9^n = 0.891)  height +inf  switch off
      near-80  main         stall     seed 12  n_tail 22  finite share 0.903 (1 - 0.9^n = 0.902)  height +inf  switch on
      near-80  random_rows  no_stall  seed  3  n_tail 28  finite share 0.948 (1 - 0.9^n = 0.948)  height +inf  switch off
      near-80  near80       no_stall  seed  3  n_tail 29  finite share 0.947 (1 - 0.9^n = 0.953)  height +inf  switch off
      near-80  random_rows  stall     seed  0  n_tail 29  finite share 0.950 (1 - 0.9^n = 0.953)  height 5.609  switch on
      step 1   main         no_stall  seed  3  n_tail 29  finite share 0.947 (1 - 0.9^n = 0.953)  height +inf  switch off
      near-80  main         stall     seed 14  n_tail 30  finite share 0.964 (1 - 0.9^n = 0.958)  height 4.595  switch on
      Count: infinite in 8 of 40; every tail of 28 or fewer refused, every tail of 30 or more certified;
      at exactly 29 rows 2 of 3 refused (a 70/30 draw: P(at least 950 of 1,000 finite) with p = 1 - 0.9^29 = 0.953).
  (b) The same arithmetic widens before it refuses: Bayesian margin lambda_hpd/lambda_hat on random subsets of the recorded
      scores, n = 300: 1.17; n = 100: 1.50; full bank: 1.089.
  (c) The IW arms with exact weights never refused a row: weighting test R2 refused_rows = 0 on 25 of 25 seeds; four-learner
      refused_rows_last = 0 on 10 of 10 CQL seeds (18 of 18 refreshes certified).
  (d) Where weighting does refuse: the command-weighted band (weights for the actor's own commands; exploratory,
      outputs/shift_iw/explore/channel/results/command_band/<q>.json). Per seed: Kish share of the held-out rows, share of
      the actor's within-80% (IID-like) commands refused, past-80% refused, largest finite threshold / R_u:
